# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but its build
# script runs under WSL/Linux. Without the rule below, git hands the working
# copy a CRLF version of scripts/build-wasm.sh, bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r`
# as an option named "pipefail\r", and the build dies with an error that says
# nothing about line endings. `npm run wasm:build` was broken this way.
#
# Anything executed by a shell must be LF regardless of platform.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts, if any are ever added, need the opposite.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binaries git should never try to normalise or diff as text. The .wasm files
# are committed build artifacts and a single stray byte breaks them.
*.wasm binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated, and large: keep it out of diffs where it only adds noise.
src/surrogate/model.json -diff
package-lock.json -diff

# wasm-pack output: machine-generated, only ever read by tooling, and rewritten
# in full on every build. Pinning to LF keeps rebuilds from showing as changes
# purely because the working copy was checked out with CRLF.
crates/burn-core/pkg-node/** text eol=lf
crates/burn-core/pkg-web/** text eol=lf
crates/burn-core/pkg-node/*.wasm binary
crates/burn-core/pkg-web/*.wasm binary
